      "text": [
        " قَالَ عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : فِي رَجُلٍ يَكُونُ لَهُ مَالٌ عَلَى رَجُلٍ فَيَتَقَاضَاهُ وَ لاَ يَكُونُ عِنْدَهُ مَا يَقْضِيهِ فَيَقُولُ هُوَ عِنْدَكَ مُضَارَبَةً قَالَ \"لاَ يَصْلُحُ حَتَّى يَقْبِضَهُ مِنْهُ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3845 - Al-Sakooni narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), from his forefathers (peace be upon them) who said that Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) said regarding a man who is owed money by another man and demands repayment, but the debtor does not have the means to repay and says, \"Consider it as a partnership investment with you.\"\nImam (as) said: \"It is not permissible until he first takes possession of it from him.\""
        ]
      }
    },
